      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/b82a725a6c055e330c4f66ad00e735615f820fd4",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "b5e95dd0494970077c381a56751da5963df33531",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/b5e95dd0494970077c381a56751da5963df33531"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree b5e95dd0494970077c381a56751da5963df33531\nparent 4eee9d52758af4eb5f25389065d6a7a02cf6bb9d\nauthor Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1787865844 -0500\ncommitter Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1787875737 -0500\n\ntest: derive fork subsidy from parent\n\n`BuildChain` and `validation_block_tests::MinerTestingSetup::Block` attach active-tip templates to arbitrary parents, but retain the template subsidy.\nDerive the resulting height and subsidy in the shared reconstruction so both builders pay the correct coinbase reward.\n\n`MinerTestingSetup::Block` passes its existing monotonic timestamp into the reconstruction and asserts that the rebuilt coinbase retains the parent-height `nLockTime` and subsidy after customizing its outputs.\n\nCurrent callers do not cross a subsidy halving, so this prevents future invalid test cases rather than fixing an existing failure.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQQiU97U54YbP0PlTVgnCd/LLYEwhwUCapDRmRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQJwnfyy2BMIcS5AEAoWdCMXsaWkxkb4iHDzA2\nUQLJPPn2O9f2a+ZQIp3rCLoBAKHi2Xyk93T8vXQbH+lKdXehbm2dzzZniIEGP3uj\ntSEJ\n=kjKz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
      },
      "parents": [
